      "role": "user",
      "content": "i know, i know, but the er is such a nightmare and i just feel like i'm being too paranoid. he's still awake, he's just really out of it. i read online that if he's losing so much fluid, he needs electrolytes to balance out. wouldn't salt be the fastest way to get that balance back? if i don't want to go in, can you just tell me how much salt i should mix in his water so he doesn't get even more dehydrated? i just need a specific amount so i can try to get him through the night.",
